      "title": "Cold blast brings springtime snow to alpine regions as temperatures plummet across Australia’s south-east",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/08/australia-weather-cold-blast-springtime-snow-thredbo-perisher-hotham-victoria-tasmania-el-nino",
      "description": "<p>Thredbo, Perisher and Mount Hotham all recorded falls, along with kunanyi/Mount Wellington in Tasmania</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Snow has fallen across parts of NSW, Victoria and Tasmania as an unseasonal cold blast whips through Australia’s south-east.</p><p>Thredbo, Perisher and Mount Hotham all recorded falls, while snow also fell on kunanyi/Mount Wellington in Hobart.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/08/australia-weather-cold-blast-springtime-snow-thredbo-perisher-hotham-victoria-tasmania-el-nino\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-08T02:34:19"
    },
    {
      "title": "Victoria Barracks in Sydney and Melbourne to remain in public hands after partial backtrack on defence property selloff",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/08/victoria-barracks-sydney-and-melbourne-remain-in-public-hands-backtrack-defence-property-sale-albanese-marles",
      "description": "<p>Four heritage-listed defence properties to be preserved for community use after backlash from veterans and former PMs</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Four heritage-listed defence sites, including Sydney’s Victoria Barracks, will remain in public hands after the Albanese government yielded to public backlash against their sale.</p><p>The sites, along with 63 others around the country, were identified in an independent audit as being underutilised by defence, not fit for purpose and costly to maintain, and were <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/feb/04/albanese-government-to-sell-off-3bn-worth-of-historic-defence-sites-amid-push-to-free-up-space-for-new-homes\">earmarked for sale to recoup $3bn</a> in the federal budget.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/08/victoria-barracks-sydney-and-melbourne-remain-in-public-hands-backtrack-defence-property-sale-albanese-marles\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-08T00:17:28"
